---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { getTranslations } from '../../lib/i18n';

const lang = 'en';
const t = getTranslations(lang);
---

<Layout lang={lang} title="Copyright Policy & Takedown Requests" description="Fair use principles, ethical content aggregation standards, and instant removal guidelines.">
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto bg-[var(--bg-surface)] border border-[var(--border-color)] rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-10 shadow-craft mb-12">
    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="pb-6 border-b border-[var(--border-subtle)] mb-8">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-md bg-[var(--accent-bg)] text-[var(--accent)] border border-[var(--accent-border)] text-xs font-mono font-semibold mb-3">
        <span>⚖️ Legal Compliance & Fair Use</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-serif font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">
        Copyright Policy & Takedown Notice
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
        We firmly respect the intellectual property rights of creators, bloggers, and online publications.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-sm sm:text-base text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-serif font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">
          1. Aggregator Model (Fair Use & Direct Linking)
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-3">
          Tech Tips Hub operates purely as an indexer and directory:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-xs sm:text-sm pl-2">
          <li><strong>No Full Article Reproduction:</strong> We never copy or reproduce entire articles. We store only brief excerpts (1-2 sentences) and normalized headlines.</li>
          <li><strong>Direct Canonical Attribution:</strong> Every entry contains an explicit, prominent "Read Original" link driving readership directly back to the original publisher.</li>
          <li><strong>No Media Scraping:</strong> We do not download or host original author images, attachments, or videos.</li>
          <li><strong>Robots.txt & RSS Adherence:</strong> Our crawlers read public feeds and respect standard web etiquette and rate limits.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-serif font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">
          2. Machine Translation Notice
        </h2>
        <p>
          Bilingual titles and summaries are generated via automated machine translation models to aid cross-linguistic discovery. The original publication remains the authoritative, definitive reference for all technical instructions.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-serif font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">
          3. Takedown & Content Removal Requests
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-3">
          If you are an author or publisher and prefer that your feed or specific articles not be referenced on Tech Tips Hub, we will swiftly honor your request:
        </p>
        <div class="p-5 rounded-xl border border-[var(--border-color)] bg-[var(--bg-muted)] space-y-3">
          <p class="font-semibold text-xs sm:text-sm text-[var(--text-primary)]">
            How to request removal:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5 text-xs">
            <li>Open a <strong>GitHub Issue</strong> on our public repository tagged with <code class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-[var(--bg-surface)] font-mono">takedown-request</code>.</li>
            <li>Specify the article URL or full domain you wish excluded.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-xs text-[var(--text-muted)]">
            Upon receipt, your domain or URL pattern will be appended to <code class="font-mono">config/blocklist.yml</code>, permanently pruning your content in the subsequent automated build.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
